---
description: Conventions for the ralph-sandbox repository. Always on.
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the instructions in @AGENTS.md. It is the single source of truth for
this repository, shared with Claude Code, Codex and Copilot; do not add rules
here, add them there.

The parts that bite most often:

- The sandbox boundary is the product. Nothing new enters the container
  (mounts, environment variables, networks, allowlist hosts) without README
  text and a CI test.
- Host scripts (`ralph`, `install.sh`) must run on bash 3.2. ASCII only.
  shellcheck warning-free. `set -euo pipefail` stays.
- Comments say why, not what. Match the voice of `loop.sh` and the README.
- Conventional Commits, one change per commit. Never rewrite history.
- Leave `templates/` alone unless the task is about them.
